    "items": [
      {
        "type": "heading1",
        "verse_numbers": [],
        "lines": [
          "Job Continues: I Will Maintain My Integrity"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          1
        ],
        "lines": [
          "And Job again took up his discourse, and said:"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          2
        ],
        "lines": [
          "“As God lives, who has taken away my right,",
          "and the Almighty, who has made my soul bitter,"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          3
        ],
        "lines": [
          "as long as my breath is in me,",
          "and the spirit of God is in my nostrils,"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          4
        ],
        "lines": [
          "my lips will not speak falsehood,",
          "and my tongue will not utter deceit."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          5
        ],
        "lines": [
          "Far be it from me to say that you are right;",
          "till I die I will not put away my integrity from me."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          6
        ],
        "lines": [
          "I hold fast my righteousness and will not let it go;",
          "my heart does not reproach me for any of my days."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          7
        ],
        "lines": [
          "“Let my enemy be as the wicked,",
          "and let him who rises up against me be as the unrighteous."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          8
        ],
        "lines": [
          "For what is the hope of the godless when God cuts him off,",
          "when God takes away his life?"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          9
        ],
        "lines": [
          "Will God hear his cry",
          "when distress comes upon him?"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          10
        ],
        "lines": [
          "Will he take delight in the Almighty?",
          "Will he call upon God at all times?"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          11
        ],
        "lines": [
          "I will teach you concerning the hand of God;",
          "what is with the Almighty I will not conceal."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          12
        ],
        "lines": [
          "Behold, all of you have seen it yourselves;",
          "why then have you become altogether vain?"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          13
        ],
        "lines": [
          "“This is the portion of a wicked man with God,",
          "and the heritage that oppressors receive from the Almighty:"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          14
        ],
        "lines": [
          "If his children are multiplied, it is for the sword,",
          "and his descendants have not enough bread."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          15
        ],
        "lines": [
          "Those who survive him the pestilence buries,",
          "and his widows do not weep."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          16
        ],
        "lines": [
          "Though he heap up silver like dust,",
          "and pile up clothing like clay,"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          17
        ],
        "lines": [
          "he may pile it up, but the righteous will wear it,",
          "and the innocent will divide the silver."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          18
        ],
        "lines": [
          "He builds his house like a moth’s,",
          "like a booth that a watchman makes."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          19
        ],
        "lines": [
          "He goes to bed rich, but will do so no more;",
          "he opens his eyes, and his wealth is gone."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          20
        ],
        "lines": [
          "Terrors overtake him like a flood;",
          "in the night a whirlwind carries him off."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          21
        ],
        "lines": [
          "The east wind lifts him up and he is gone;",
          "it sweeps him out of his place."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          22
        ],
        "lines": [
          "It hurls at him without pity;",
          "he flees from its power in headlong flight."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          23
        ],
        "lines": [
          "It claps its hands at him",
          "and hisses at him from its place."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      }
    ]
  },
